  "body": "## What changed\n\nCircular Ramp entries stay at depth between eligible levels of one ring.\nThe generator uses the existing certified KeepDown link.\nEach new ring still enters from clearance.\nThe final retract stays in place.\n\nThe first ramp starts at most 0.1 mm above the remaining material.\nA smaller configured gap stays in use.\nThe remaining material height keeps the rapid above stock over Top Z.\nExplicit Retract links and other transition types keep their selected lift planes.\nRamp-to-depth entries keep their lift behavior.\n\nThe decision is in `docs/decisions/1807-circular-stay-down.md`.\nEffort: high.\n\n## Cause\n\nCircular passed the default Clearance link to every level transition.\nThe default 2 mm entry gap also made the first ramp travel through excess air.\nReadings: the local Circular generator, level-link proof, descent planner, and Approach material-height contract.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe two primary pins failed on unchanged upstream code:\n\n- `circular_ramp_stays_down_between_levels_of_one_ring`: 12 upward rapid moves instead of one.\n- `circular_first_ramp_starts_just_above_material`: entry began 2 mm above material instead of within 0.1 mm.\n\nThe motion suite now passes all six tests.\nThe pins cover both cut directions and implicit or explicit Ramp transitions.\nThey also cover smaller entry gaps and alternative link choices.\n\n`circular_stay_down_keeps_stock_entry_safe_and_does_not_gouge` passes four cases.\nIt tests one or two rings in both directions with stock above Top Z.\nVerification accepts each path.\nStock simulation reports zero gouge cells.\n`circular_ramp_stay_down_matches_golden` also passes.\n\nThe full old-code replacement fails both primary pins.\nSeven separate mutations fail their matching assertions:\n\n- Remove the Ramp entry guard.\n- Remove the Clearance link guard.\n- Remove the Ramp transition guard.\n- Remove the ramp-to-depth guard.\n- Discard a smaller entry gap.\n- Remove the 0.1 mm cap.\n- Remove the KeepDown selection.\n\nAll pins pass after each restoration.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed 630 steps with zero failures.\nThe new shared CL fixture made the gate select the broader fixture consumers.\n`import_step_guard` passed without a retry.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\nThe tested branch starts at upstream commit `3970d3d0319e423761c48f9a7e0a6391a14b9403`.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nAdded `crates/app/tests/golden/circular_ramp_stay_down.cl`.\nThe existing Circular Helix golden has no change.\nNo `.nc` file changes.\n\nThe old generator emits 185 moves for the new fixture.\nThe fixed generator emits 133 moves.\nThe comparison changes only the initial air ramps, intermediate clearance rapid pairs, and the move count.\nCut rings, interlevel descent arcs, ring changes, and the final retract stay identical.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nPhysical CNC hardware, the PathPilot simulator, and release-only heavy tests did not run.\nLater upstream changes were not merged into this branch.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone at the file checks before the claim.\nPR #1713, which blocked the previous attempt, had already merged.\n\nChangelog: Circular Ramp entries stay at depth between levels and start near the remaining material.\n\nFixes #1807\n",
